TBD - 0.3
- Receives QSOs from KLog and stores the data in an ADIF file. KLog sends the QSOs
  that are logged as an ADIF record with all the fields that have data and the record
  is saved just as it is received, so no ADIF field is lost. The datagram has the same
  layout that WSJT-X uses, with the magic number 1999030602 that identifies KLog.
- Bugfix: The N1MM parser did not build with Qt6.

Mar 2026 - 0.2
- Migrated to Qt6

Nov 2022 - 0.1
- First "release" of the software.
- Receives QSOs from N1MM and stores the data in an ADIF file.
- Receives QSOs from WSJTX and stores the data in an ADIF file.
